{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542291-herding-cats-range-bands-and-positioning","id":1542291,"title":"Herding Cats (Range Bands and Positioning)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-16T20:28:03-07:00","id":1542291,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Herding Cats (Range Bands and Positioning)","content":"I've been playing TRPGs for close to 30 years and I've noticed a shift from feet/meters/squares/fixed units to range bands. I understand the concept of fist/shotgun/rifle/artillery/ICBM range but how do you track positions?<br /> <br /> For example, Person A is Medium for Person B and Long for Person C. Person B is also Long for Person C.<br /> <br /> Person A moves from Medium to Short to Person B. How does this affect Person A's position to Person C?<br /> <br /> It seems like any time someone changes bands, you have to recalculate the new band distance to everyone, not just the active character and their destination/target.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's a simple answer that I'm missing but after reading at least three different games' Core books, I haven't found one that explained positioning in a way I comprehend.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T23:53:19-07:00","id":1542297,"title":"","content":"<b>Storypath Ultru Core Manual</b> solves your problem - I'm not sure those rules will be printed in <b>Curseborne</b> core, but they are in <b>SP Ultra</b> one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SP Ultra Core Chapter 2</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Distance for Virtual Tabletop</b><br /> The distances described in the range table are narrative depictions to give some basis for the range bands. When playing the game using a virtual tabletop, narrative ranges aren\u2019t as useful as actual distances. The following table gives hard distances and converts them to squares for VTT play.<br /> <br /> <b>Range - Typical Distance - VTT Squares</b><br /> <b>Close </b>0-2 meters 1 square<br /> <b>Short</b> 3-20 meters 2-10 squares<br /> <b>Medium </b>21-60 meters 11-30 squares<br /> <b>Long</b> Over 60 meters to maximum effective range, ~1,000 meters 30-~500 squares<br /> <b>Extreme</b> By Situation (typically 1,000+ meters) n/a<br /> <b>Out of Range</b> Beyond maximum weapon range n/a</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-12-2024, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T06:52:56-07:00","id":1542310,"title":"","content":"My experience in SP is as a narrative game more than a table top game. I usually use a simple rule:<br /> Close = touching range<br /> Short = within the same room in a house or equivalent<br /> Medium = not the same room but within the same football field or equivalent.<br /> Long = further than a football field but you can still see clearly.<br /> Extreme = need a binocular or other helps to see clearly.<br /> <br /> Most of times the characters remain basically within the same range bands all the scene, except if they sprint around. So usually only what is within close or short range change, if you sprint to the location of others within medium range you can change what is in medium range. But you can hardly change what\u2019s in long distance unless you have a car (or is super fast, what is also possible) and it can run freely in a large space (kilometers long and wide)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-17-2024, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T06:54:04-07:00","id":1542311,"title":"","content":"Double post. Please delete if possible","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T17:16:23-07:00","id":1542343,"title":"","content":"Thank you, wyrdhamster, for that table from the SP Core.<br /> <br /> Mateus Luz, those seem like good descriptors. Can't characters move from Medium to Close as a single action, though? Moving a whole football field and still being able to make a melee attack seems like a lot without the use of some kind of special ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T19:11:38-07:00","id":1542347,"title":"","content":"The general idea is you can move 1 range band for free, so you can take a few steps easily with no effort. <br /> You can use an action (that can be part of an mixed action) to move another range band, so you can move anywhere within a room as part of a mixed action.<br /> To move another range band you need to have an speed advantage, in TC you have Edges for that, in Scion you have knacks, things people can reach on the lowest playable character level. So you can, if you have the proper abilities, move to medium range as a part of a mixed action. A character without that special traits won\u2019t be able to move to medium range in combat.<br /> <br /> To go further you need powers\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T00:03:27-07:00","id":1542355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542291-herding-cats-range-bands-and-positioning?p=1542347#post1542347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general idea is you can move 1 range band for free, so you can take a few steps easily with no effort.<br /> You can use an action (that can be part of an mixed action) to move another range band, so you can move anywhere within a room as part of a mixed action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, this is a bit weird if you go by set up VTT measures...<br /> <br /> If <b>Short</b> is <i>'up to 20 meters'</i> and <b>Medium</b> is <i>'up to 60 meters' </i>- You take just one turn to move first 20 meters, and then on next turn you move 40 meteres. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i><b>I would go </b></i><b>CoD </b><i><b>route here</b></i> - in <b>CoD</b> characters have <b>Speed 10 meters per turn on basis. 20 meters when 'Running' action.</b> This would be much more logical. Then you would leave Medium band in 2 turns, not one, and only when sacrificing action on each turn ( 40 m = 2 *20 meters ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <b>Speed Advantage 1</b> would give you 20 m base move, 40 m Running. <b>Speed Advantage 2</b> give 40 m base move, 80 m Running. Etc.<br /> <br /> I already run <b>Trinity Continuum</b> by those rules by 2 years and they work fine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-18-2024, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T09:41:39-07:00","id":1542373,"title":"","content":"It seems awful early to be complaining about the rules and suggesting house rules when the game isn't even in Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T12:04:49-07:00","id":1542381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542291-herding-cats-range-bands-and-positioning?p=1542373#post1542373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems awful early to be complaining about the rules and suggesting house rules when the game isn't even in Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/projects/onyx-path/storypath-ultra-rules-manual\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Storypath Ultra rules</b> I quoted are already on Backerkit.</a> And yes, we are divided in reactions to those, at least on <b>TC DIscord</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T14:04:46-07:00","id":1542392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542291-herding-cats-range-bands-and-positioning?p=1542381#post1542381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/projects/onyx-path/storypath-ultra-rules-manual\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Storypath Ultra rules</b> I quoted are already on Backerkit.</a> And yes, we are divided in reactions to those, at least on <b>TC DIscord</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for the generic storypath are released on backerkit, yes, that's different than the actual game being released. No game follows the generic rules exactly, see Dungeon World / Apocalypse World for an example of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T14:35:43-07:00","id":1543638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542291-herding-cats-range-bands-and-positioning?p=1542347#post1542347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general idea is you can move 1 range band for free, so you can take a few steps easily with no effort.<br /> You can use an action (that can be part of an mixed action) to move another range band, so you can move anywhere within a room as part of a mixed action.<br /> To move another range band you need to have an speed advantage, in TC you have Edges for that, in Scion you have knacks, things people can reach on the lowest playable character level. So you can, if you have the proper abilities, move to medium range as a part of a mixed action. A character without that special traits won\u2019t be able to move to medium range in combat.<br /> <br /> To go further you need powers\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for replying to an old thread but I've been curious about this since Exalted: Essence.<br /> <br /> This makes sense, but it's no my reading if the rules. The rule doesn't say &quot;move anywhere in Close range of your current location&quot; it says &quot;move one range band&quot;. To me (and I think to the OP) that means if something is at Long range from you, you can use the free move action to get one range band closer, bringing it into Medium range.<br /> <br /> Now I agree that's a silly and confusing way to do it but it does seem to be the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T20:23:48-07:00","id":1543662,"title":"","content":"Range bands are functional (if unrealistic) for one-on-one combat, but collapse when you introduce a third person.<br /> <br /> My preference would be Fate Core's method. Divide every area into zones. Everything in the same zone is Close range. You can move to an adjacent zone for free, and adjacent zones are in Short range. If you spend your action running you can move two zones. Medium, Long and Extreme ranges are progressively longer paths of zones. You do need a map to use that system, but not a complicated one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T07:20:22-07:00","id":1543677,"title":"","content":"The focus of my interpretation at least is scale and how the characters can move around those distances.<br /> Each range band is 10-ish times larger than the one before, so it\u2019s something like: 3 feet, 30 feet, 300 feet, 3000 feet.<br /> That is like that because not only the character is using better weapons but also because the characters in Storypath can be much faster than other people, crossing kilometers in a round.<br /> <br /> I personally do something like Fate Core, but not exactly. The thing here is more about what you can move and what you can\u2019t, if you have 2 \u201cplaces to fight\u201d, like 2 groups of adversaries or 2 independent adversaries that don\u2019t want to be close to each other you just set the distance between them as a determined number of range bands and to move between them you need to cross that gap. If tou can all move and you all want to be at close range, than you are probably going to be in 2 rounds max.<br /> <br /> Can you cross a \u201c3 range bands distance\u201d by moving 2 range bands each time? Yes, but it will take 10-ish rounds, so why bother? That can be basically an entire scene, as combats in SP lasts usually less than 10 rounds.<br /> Same for pushing a person against his will to cross a \u201c2 range bands distance\u201d 1 range band each time, it takes longer than take one out here, go there and take the other out.<br /> <br /> But I need to punch that guy that is being shooting me with a sniper rifle, I want to cross the entire space! Than you have a scene for that, one that the characters are avoiding being shot while moving, with each action representing a part of the distance covered, possibly with some difficulties to cross barriers or difficult terrain and a complication that if not bought off means you got shot. Same for the opposite, you have one guy running away from the others, you change scene to a chasing scene, with its own challenges and narrative aspects.<br /> <br /> That takes us to what is a scene. From TC Core:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scene: This is the amount of time it takes for<br /> an entire set of related actions to occur. This<br /> could be anywhere from a few minutes to an<br /> hour. Scenes encompass all the action for a sin-<br /> gle thing, so a car chase is a scene, an interro-<br /> gation is a scene, and a firefight is a scene. But if<br /> a firefight transitions into a foot chase then the<br /> scene changes when the action changes. </div> </div> </div>It means, by the rules, you have a scene for approaching the shooting adversary and a scene for fighting the adversary if you are not able to cross the entire distance in a feasible time. Or you break the scene when you start running away (you break the scene for you and those that are chasing you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 10-13-2024, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T08:23:30-07:00","id":1543682,"title":"","content":"Right I get why you interpret it that way. What I'm questioning is whether that is *actually what the rules are*.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, if you can move 2 range bands in a round, you can cross 4 range bands in two rounds. Otherwise you're not really using range bands at all, you're just using distances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T09:43:50-07:00","id":1543685,"title":"","content":"I guess we can wait for some official answers\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T10:47:04-07:00","id":1543694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542291-herding-cats-range-bands-and-positioning?p=1543685#post1543685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess we can wait for some official answers\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Aah, having checked the Curseborne Ashcan it's actually much clearer than I was giving it credit for. It says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Move: Characters can move between Close<br /> and Short or Short and Medium as a reflexive<br /> action. A character can run as a simple action to<br /> move between Close and Medium range. </div> </div> </div>Then there's a Rush action to move from Medium to Close and attack. This *does* mean you definitely can attack somebody 60m away in one turn but that's not actually hugely awkward but there's definitely no fixed action to move to or from Long range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T03:51:18-07:00","id":1543969,"title":"","content":"Yea, the range band thing doesn't really work with multiple participants. Hopefully they clean this up before they start releasing the final versions of the SP Ultra books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T03:56:05-07:00","id":1543971,"title":"","content":"I will say that as long as movement is expressed in terms of &quot;from band x to band y&quot; it's not that bad even with multiple participants, it's functionally not that different to just using distances.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately some Motifs still use the &quot;one range band&quot; language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T04:51:02-07:00","id":1543973,"title":"","content":"If you didn\u2019t notice they have the \u201csquares\u201d option in the system, so they fixed it.<br /> <br /> But to be fair it works far better in narrative than you are saying, it is just a little change in the way you see the battlefield. It\u2019s more about how you describe and less about positioning pieces in the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T05:13:56-07:00","id":1543975,"title":"","content":"It works in narrative as long as it's written the way it's written in the movement rules of the Ashcan/SPU so you can only realistically move from short to medium. <br /> <br /> It gets a lot worse when it just talks in absolute numbers of range bands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T06:28:08-07:00","id":1543978,"title":"","content":"I agree to certain level. The problem is when you start to getting faster and moving more range bands. Then if for each speed advantage you have you must describe the range band by name it gets complicated.<br /> <br /> when you translate in your head 1 range band is close range, 2 is short and so on it gets automatically translated and you describes it to the players as you prefer<br /> <br /> Personally I don\u2019t like the description centered in the target instead in you (you move from short to close range). I prefer centered in your current position (you move anywhere within shot range. So it\u2019s a bit weird to me to read the text you prefer. But I am used to Storypath for a while and have written some books using it, so I probably have internalized the rules by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 10-16-2024, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T07:24:10-07:00","id":1543983,"title":"","content":"To be clear I'm also fine with PC-centric language (&quot;anywhere within short range&quot; would be fine) but that has mild problems with relative positioning (if I'm at Medium range of somebody and I move to a position within short range towards them an I still at Medium or now at Short).<br /> <br /> I have a problem with numeric regents because I think adding linear numbers for logarithmic range bands gets silly fast. Moving +1 Range Band effectively means moving 10x as far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T16:51:26-07:00","id":1544240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542291-herding-cats-range-bands-and-positioning?p=1543662#post1543662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Range bands are functional (if unrealistic) for one-on-one combat, but collapse when you introduce a third person.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's not just me seeing this?<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542291-herding-cats-range-bands-and-positioning?p=1543983#post1543983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear I'm also fine with PC-centric language (&quot;anywhere within short range&quot; would be fine) but that has mild problems with relative positioning (if I'm at Medium range of somebody and I move to a position within short range towards them an I still at Medium or now at Short).</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here is what I'm seeking clarity on, especially for combat involving multiple people.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Man and the Beast are having an amiable picnic in that Savage\u2019s head. It\u2019s rather disturbing.&quot; <i>- Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle, pg. 22</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/145-jsm3050","name":"JSM3050","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T17:56:01-07:00","id":1544243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSM3050</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542291-herding-cats-range-bands-and-positioning?p=1544240#post1544240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This right here is what I'm seeking clarity on, especially for combat involving multiple people.</div> </div> </div> </div>So *most* of the time the rules are pretty clear where one person is involved, movement is target-centric so you're moving from medium to short or short to close relative to that person.<br /> <br /> For multiple combatants, assuming you're not using a VTT (in which case you just do squares as described upthread) you are, as I understand it, just kinda meant to eyeball it. How satisfying that answer is is very much a YMMV thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T00:43:19-07:00","id":1544265,"title":"","content":"The range bands will most often come up in combat. If you spend two of your actions fleeing and nobody stops you, then congratulations: you're out of range and just as you can't be hit, neither can they. There may of course be obstacles or obstructions preventing this movement, which is why white room playtests serve very little purpose.<br /> <br /> If you're trying to flee and your attacker is pursuing you, they get to move just as you do. So while it may sound strange to move up to medium range, if your attacker decides &quot;I'm going to move up to medium range too&quot; then congratulations: effectively, you've both moved the same distance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T07:19:12-07:00","id":1544291,"title":"","content":"And are range bands meant to be measured individual to individual or are characters grouped into bands together? Like if I move &quot;up to medium&quot; am I now in medium with all the characters who were previously in medium? Or am I moving to medium relative to where I was? Or to medium away from another character who was previously at Close?<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> The way I *think* it works, just going by the movement rules in the Ashcan is that effectively any given character can be in one of five positions relative to your character:<br /> <br /> Close - You are near enough to physically touch them. If you want to attack them you can just use your action for it. <br /> <br /> Short - You aren't near enough to touch them but you can *get* near enough with a reflexive action. If you want to attack them you make a reflective action to move then a standard action to attack.<br /> <br /> Medium - Far enough away that you have to spend your whole turn moving to get into Close range. You *can* attack somebody at this distance but only by making a &quot;rush&quot; which is always rolled on Might + Athletics and seems intend to represent a kind of desperation body check not a considered attack with a weapon.<br /> <br /> Long - this is where I think it might get unintuitive for some people. As I read it, because range bands are effectively on a log scale, if somebody is a Long range then under default movement rules you can *never* get into Close range with them in a standard fight. Effectively you need to have a different sort of Scene to close the distance then so the fight afterwards.<br /> <br /> Extreme - See Long bit more so.<br /> <br /> To put it another way, the movement rules effectively divide characters into exactly two groups: the ones you can reach in a single combat round and the ones you can never reasonably reach. <br /> <br /> I think this is what makes the system traceable with multiple combatants, for any given person a PC might want to get up close and personal with there's only really two options: &quot;you can't&quot; or &quot;you can get there in a turn&quot;. It's abstract but it means you don't really have to track anything. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-19-2024, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T09:55:54-07:00","id":1544298,"title":"","content":"Adding this as a separate post because it'll probably be long, but I think it's a decent example of how this is meant to work and also what Matthew might be talking about when he says that the system's not designed for white room scenarios.<br /> <br /> Version 1:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Storyguide</b>: Okay there are three Zombie flesh eaters coming your way. Also, like always, you're in a totally featureless white void. The Zombies are currently at medium range.<br /> <br /> <b>PC1 </b>Okay, Zombies are pretty slow and we have guns and they don't. Standard strategy is retreat under fire. I move back 10 meters and shoot a zombie.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyguide</b> Right you hit the zombie but don't incapacitate it. Moving back 10 meters does nothing because you're still in Medium range, the zombie rushes you and attacks, take an injury.<br /> <br /> <b>PC2 </b> Crap, that didn't work. Okay I just take my whole action to move away from the zombie as far as I possibly can.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyguide</b> Right, that still leaves you in Medium range the Zombie rushes you and you take an injury.<br /> <br /> <b>PC3 </b>I look for a different game system. </div> </div> </div>Now obviously you *can* run it like that and it *is* RAW but the game isn't designed to function well when run that way and that's not intrinsically a flaw in the game's design, most games don't work well if you don't work with them.<br /> <br /> Version 2<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Storyguide</b> The three zombie flesh eaters burst through the door of the department store you're hiding in. They're at medium range.<br /> <br /> <b>PC1</b> Okay I don't want to get rushed by these guys but I feel like if I have to actuality get something between us if I want to stop that happening. I'll move back. So reflexive action to move to a location in Short range, make sure it's behind a shelf or something, then shoot a zombie.<br /> <br /> <b>PC2 </b>I think we need to buy some time. If you give me the spotlight next I'll drag some clothes racks together to make a barricade then pull back to join you.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyguide </b>Remember that means the Zombies will probably go first next turn.<br /> <br /> <b>PCS 1 and 2</b> Probably worth it,.<br /> <br /> <b>PC3 </b>Screw this, I run, scattering crap over the floor as I go to make it harder for Zombies to follow.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyguide </b>Okay, the Zombies approach the barricade and that kind of uses their actions because they're slow and it was far forwards. Then I'm going to have one of them take an action to start clearing the barricade then I'm going to pass it back to...let's say 3, because I don't want you lot to get six turns in a row.<br /> <br /> <b>PC3</b> Cool can I get a recap of where everybody is?<br /> <br /> <b>Storyguide </b>You're medium from the Zombies, Short from your friends. They're Short from the Zombies, Close to each other, and all the Zombies are Close to each other too, what's your action? </div> </div> </div>And obviously this is an idealised scenario where the players and GM all know the system, agree about how the system works, and are cooperating to make things come out appropriately, but that's kinda his the system is meant to be used (as far as I can tell) and the rules for movement are all the same as they are in the first example. If you want to keep a melee opponent out your face you can't just kite them, you need to give them something to use their Standard Action on that isn't Rushing you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-19-2024, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T03:46:41-07:00","id":1544344,"title":"","content":"Second option is the one that make sense. The idea that they are always at medium distance is the main point here, if you can\u2019t in a round go further than medium range, getting to long range takes some time, really long time for a combat scene.<br /> <br /> Are they capable of running after you? Yes, so running will just buy you some time, they will eventually reach you if you stop to shot and they don\u2019t. And that\u2019s where the range bands are better, you don\u2019t count steps, it is or not within range. If the challenge is to reach a safe position before they get you, it\u2019s not a combat scene, it\u2019s a chase, and chases have some interesting rules to play, like throwing obstacles to the chaser and better control of the \u201cdistance\u201d you have from them, not measured in meters, but in successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T04:33:26-07:00","id":1544384,"title":"","content":"The second option is clearly better, but that was the intent of the example. It was intended as an illustration of the difference between a white room scenario and one that actually engages with what Dungeon World would have called &quot;fictional positioning&quot;.<br /> <br /> I will add though that what it was *also* attempting to illustrate is quite how acute the problems get if you don't engage with fictional positioning and rely (as you can in many other games) on the abstract rules of the combat system to protect you. <br /> <br /> In most games it's possible through *pure rules text* to put yourself in a position where you can shoot at a melee threat and they can't close the distance and attack you in a single turn, possibly for several turns.<br /> <br /> It's not just that if your enemy can run and you back up shooting that they will catch up with you *eventually*, it's that no matter what you do, no matter how you move, there is no purely game mechanical way to stop an enemy reaching you in a single turn and making a melee attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}